From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:42:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Group compute doorbells away from
 render by default

g16_compute_bell_group, g16_compute_bell_late and
g16_compute_bell_solo_us are 0 by default, so every compute publication
rings its own doorbell and the firmware scheduler is called once per
compute command, also when a client keeps eight or more compute
commands queued. compute.light at 8 queued measured 29.1 us per
dispatch on 1.1125, 93.5 % of the 27.2 us macOS measures on this Mac.

Make 4, 1 and 100000 the defaults. A compute publication made behind
four or more compute commands in flight posts its record without
ringing, and the group is paid once at the end of the publish pass.
Grouping is set aside, and every compute record rings as before, for
100 ms after any submission holding a render command, so a render
client and a compute client beside it see the old cadence.

On experimental 1.1128, alternating the three words between 0, 0, 0
and 4, 1, 100000 on one boot (at least four runs each), compute.light
at 8 queued measured a median of 27.96 us against 29.58 us (-5.5 %),
97.3 % of macOS. No other light or heavy cell moved by more than
1.1 %, and the GPU logged no fault.

Writing 0 to g16_compute_bell_group restores the old behaviour at
runtime.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 28 ++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index 9e34aeee09..02cb42c77c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -3357,14 +3357,14 @@ pub(crate) fn lone_ctx_skip() -> bool {
     "G16: 1 = with g16_notifier_cached, retire a render with nothing behind it without the cached record CONTEXT words; stamps, receipts and scene times still prove it (default 1; 0 holds such a render until its cached CONTEXT words are cleaned)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_compute_bell_group` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-static COMPUTE_BELL_GROUP: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_compute_bell_group` (runtime 0644, default 4).
+static COMPUTE_BELL_GROUP: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(4);
 
 /// `g16_compute_bell_group` k (2 to 16): a compute publication made while at least k compute
 /// commands are already in flight posts its record without ringing; the k-th such publication
 /// rings for all of them, so one firmware scheduler call takes the group. Any compute ring
 /// covers the owed records, and they are rung at the end of any publish pass that finds fewer
-/// than k compute commands in flight (compute_bell.rs). 0 (default) or any other value: every
+/// than k compute commands in flight (compute_bell.rs). Default 4. 0 or any other value: every
 /// compute publication rings as `g16_compute_onebell` says, as before. Read at each compute
 /// publication and publish pass.
 pub(crate) fn compute_bell_group() -> u32 {
@@ -3377,16 +3377,16 @@ pub(crate) fn compute_bell_group() -> u32 {
     COMPUTE_BELL_GROUP_PARM,
     COMPUTE_BELL_GROUP,
     "g16_compute_bell_group",
-    "G16: k = compute records behind k others ring once per k publications (2-16; default 0, off)"
+    "G16: k = compute records behind k others ring once per k publications (2-16; default 4; 0 = off)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_compute_bell_late` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-static COMPUTE_BELL_LATE: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_compute_bell_late` (runtime 0644, default 1).
+static COMPUTE_BELL_LATE: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(1);
 
 /// `g16_compute_bell_late` 1, with `g16_compute_bell_group` k: the group is paid once at the end
 /// of each publish pass that owes k or more records, instead of by the k-th deferred record
 /// inside the pass, so a pass rings at most once for its deferred records (compute_bell.rs).
-/// 0 (default) or any other value: the k-th record pays, as before. No effect while the group
+/// Default 1. 0 or any other value: the k-th record pays, as before. No effect while the group
 /// is off. Read at each compute publication and publish pass.
 pub(crate) fn compute_bell_late() -> u32 {
     u32::from(COMPUTE_BELL_LATE.load(Ordering::Relaxed) == 1)
@@ -3398,17 +3398,17 @@ pub(crate) fn compute_bell_late() -> u32 {
     COMPUTE_BELL_LATE_PARM,
     COMPUTE_BELL_LATE,
     "g16_compute_bell_late",
-    "G16: 1 = pay the compute bell group once at the end of each publish pass (default 0)"
+    "G16: 1 = pay the compute bell group once at the end of each publish pass (default 1; 0 = off)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_compute_bell_solo_us` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-static COMPUTE_BELL_SOLO_US: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_compute_bell_solo_us` (runtime 0644, default 100000).
+static COMPUTE_BELL_SOLO_US: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(100000);
 
 /// `g16_compute_bell_solo_us` = N: `g16_compute_bell_group` and `g16_compute_bell_late` act
 /// only while no submission holding a render command was made within the last N us; while one
-/// was, every compute record rings, as with the group off (compute_bell.rs). 0 (default): the
-/// two words act as set. Read at each compute publication, each publish pass end, and each
-/// submission.
+/// was, every compute record rings, as with the group off (compute_bell.rs). Default
+/// 100000. 0: the two words act as set. Read at each compute publication, each publish pass
+/// end, and each submission.
 pub(crate) fn compute_bell_solo_us() -> u32 {
     COMPUTE_BELL_SOLO_US.load(Ordering::Relaxed)
 }
@@ -3419,7 +3419,7 @@ pub(crate) fn compute_bell_solo_us() -> u32 {
     COMPUTE_BELL_SOLO_US_PARM,
     COMPUTE_BELL_SOLO_US,
     "g16_compute_bell_solo_us",
-    "G16: N > 0 = the compute bell group and late pay act only with no render submission in the last N us (default 0)"
+    "G16: N > 0 = the compute bell group and late pay act only with no render submission in the last N us (default 100000; 0 = off)"
 );
 
 /// Storage of `g16_ta_short` (runtime 0644, default 1).
-- 
2.43.0

